# Normalise text files to LF in the repository.
#
# The repo was previously mixed: most files were LF, but bot.py,
# core/server.py and core/commands.py were CRLF. Editing a CRLF file with a
# tool that writes LF rewrote every line, so an unrelated whole-file diff
# rode along inside a feature change (and reset `git blame` for that file).
# Declaring the convention here means git normalises on commit regardless of
# which editor or OS produced the file.
#
# The bot is developed and deployed on Linux; it drives servers over
# tmux/screen, RCON and POSIX signals, so LF is the right target.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted. The PNG below genuinely
# contains \r\n byte sequences in its compressed data, so it would be
# corrupted if it were ever treated as text.
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
